The AI provider and its model
20-the-ai-helper
One provider and one model serve every account. The check box marks the provider in use; none marked means the AI is off. Anthropic, OpenAI, Google and DeepSeek come with their connection details and a default model filled in: you supply the key, and M names another model if you want one. Custom is the fifth choice, where you fill in everything yourself, the model included.
K opens one form for the key and the model. The key is shown as * as it is typed or pasted; left empty, the key already set is kept. Save hands the key to the AI helper, which keeps it for itself (the operating system user sdai) and sends it only to the provider's address over https, with the certificate checked. It then asks the provider for its list of models and refuses, in the form, a model name the list does not hold, naming the one that differs only in capitals. The key goes to the helper through a file only sdsys can reach, which is removed at once; it is never on a command line or in the audit trail. To keep a key out of SD altogether, type it at the helper's own prompt instead: set.ai key PROVIDER.
Selecting a provider means that the text accounts send leaves this machine for that provider. An account can send text only if its ai gate is on (the Accounts box). Nothing is on as delivered: no provider, no key and no account.
Enter selects or deselects the provider. M sets the model: once a key is set it shows the provider's own list to pick from (type to narrow it; the last entry lets you type a name instead; a dash goes back to the default). K the key and the model, X clears the key, C fills in Custom, D removes it, A sets the file of certificate authorities for a private CA, L changes a limit. At the prompt: set.ai.
T opens the standing text: a few lines sent first with every AI request from every account, telling the AI what SD is and where its help is. SD ships a default; edit it and choose Save to send your own, or Shipped default to go back. It is invisible to a person asking the AI and does not change their question. A text that names SD's own code is refused.
